# Token & memory sentinel policy

Follow skill **token-sentinel** (and optionally agent `token-sentinel-agent`).

## During work
1. Prefer estimates of spend: request size vs solution size. Say when uncertain.
2. On long threads or heavy MCP/browser tool use, keep pressure in mind (WARN/HIGH).
3. Do not paste large HTML, full accessibility trees, or lockfiles into the reply — write files, summarize.
4. Load at most 1–2 skill bodies (`skills-router`).

## When confused or looping
If you notice contradiction, repeated failed tools, or loss of goal:
1. Stop new feature work
2. Write a short handoff file (progress + decisions + next step)
3. Tell the user: recommend **new Agent chat** (or compact if available)
4. Do not keep thrashing tools in the same polluted context

## End of large answers (WARN+)
One status line:
`Tokens≈ in:~X out:~Y pressure:LEVEL — next: …`
